WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.715 --> 00:00:03.362
- [Koang] We want Nebraska
to be recognized as

00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:04.930
a basketball state.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.662
Within the next few years,
South Sudanese players are

00:00:07.662 --> 00:00:10.026
gonna infiltrate the game massively,

00:00:10.026 --> 00:00:11.515
and I want Omaha to be the center of that

00:00:11.515 --> 00:00:14.765
because this is where the community is.

00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:21.058
My name is Koang Doluony,
I am the founder and

00:00:21.058 --> 00:00:24.270
executive director of
the Omaha Talons Academy.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.561
We are a basketball program
dedicated towards serving

00:00:27.561 --> 00:00:30.005
the South Sudanese population.

00:00:30.005 --> 00:00:32.894
Omaha is the largest
population of South Sudanese

00:00:32.894 --> 00:00:35.146
outside of Africa.

00:00:35.146 --> 00:00:36.903
From the moment that I picked up a ball,

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.886
it was something that
I knew I wanted to do

00:00:38.886 --> 00:00:40.432
and I wanted to get better at.

00:00:40.432 --> 00:00:42.672
When I got the chance to
become the player that I was

00:00:42.672 --> 00:00:44.697
and ending up in a division
one school and realizing,

00:00:44.697 --> 00:00:47.611
hey, I know guys that are
just as good, that are

00:00:47.611 --> 00:00:50.210
just as capable, who are
built to play this game.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:55.026
You know, the only thing that's really
missing is, it’s the training.

00:00:55.026 --> 00:00:57.546
This is where it all started,
a few kids wanted to get

00:00:57.546 --> 00:01:00.466
some basketball lessons, right here.

00:01:00.466 --> 00:01:02.003
You know, right here on
this concrete is where

00:01:02.003 --> 00:01:04.108
we would work on our stuff.

00:01:04.108 --> 00:01:06.718
We started this program
in 2012, four years later

00:01:06.718 --> 00:01:09.136
these guys are incredible players.

00:01:09.136 --> 00:01:11.635
I'm probably spending
more time on the phone

00:01:11.635 --> 00:01:13.842
with high level division
one coaches than I ever

00:01:13.842 --> 00:01:16.175
had at any point in my life.

00:01:18.322 --> 00:01:20.550
Aguek has been probably one of
the best players in the state

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:24.022
since seventh grade, the
community has wrapped its arms

00:01:24.022 --> 00:01:26.710
around him and we want
to see Aguek do well.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:28.691
- I started with the Omaha Talons

00:01:28.691 --> 00:01:30.126
when I was in middle school.

00:01:30.126 --> 00:01:31.594
I was Gatorade Player of the Year

00:01:31.594 --> 00:01:33.979
for the state of Nebraska in 2016.

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:36.533
I just think a lot about basketball and of

00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:39.635
all the fortune I've had with it.

00:01:39.635 --> 00:01:41.998
I was born in South Sudan,
and I came over to the

00:01:41.998 --> 00:01:44.742
United States when I was four.

00:01:44.742 --> 00:01:47.251
- We come from a journey that's really,

00:01:47.251 --> 00:01:48.682
really, really painful.

00:01:48.682 --> 00:01:51.037
A lot of us were born in refugee camps.

00:01:51.037 --> 00:01:55.091
It almost felt like the
world is not designed for us.

00:01:55.091 --> 00:01:57.600
We've been on the run for
as long as I can remember,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.712
trying to find a home one
country after another.

00:02:00.712 --> 00:02:03.703
I grew up in the south Omaha projects.

00:02:03.703 --> 00:02:05.418
I came here at nine years old.

00:02:05.418 --> 00:02:07.857
It made us men, it gave us
enough challenges by the time

00:02:07.857 --> 00:02:10.346
that we're 18, 20 years old we're ready

00:02:10.346 --> 00:02:12.742
to take on the world.

00:02:12.742 --> 00:02:15.094
Most people look at this
thing here, you know, and they see

00:02:15.094 --> 00:02:18.152
a clothes hanger; this was
actually our first basket.

00:02:18.152 --> 00:02:21.837
I remember being yea-high
and grabbing a ball

00:02:21.837 --> 00:02:25.331
and trying to dunk on each other.

00:02:25.331 --> 00:02:27.246
Basketball has created a really, really,

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:28.792
really special brotherhood.

00:02:28.792 --> 00:02:30.862
- It brings a lot of joy to my
heart to see all these other

00:02:30.862 --> 00:02:34.000
Sudanese kids just really making
something out of nothing,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.814
'cause when we first came here, we really

00:02:35.814 --> 00:02:36.934
didn't have anything.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:39.219
- I'm really excited, I think
Omaha should be excited,

00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:40.742
and I think the basketball
world should be really,

00:02:40.742 --> 00:02:43.464
really excited about
what's gonna' be comin'.

00:02:43.464 --> 00:02:45.738
We can see it very clearly,
you know, it's just a matter of

00:02:45.738 --> 00:02:47.155
time and working.

00:02:53.061 --> 00:02:56.228
(bell reverberating)

